<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
	Definition overlay for the "optimized" profile.

	This file is NOT a definition file. It lives outside Data/ deliberately: everything under
	Data/ is loaded by the game and by Definition Extensions, and a second copy of Cubes.xml
	there would collide with the first. The mod reads this itself, when this profile is in
	force, and applies it over what the definitions loaded.

	What an overlay is for: a block's demand on the integrator is its conductance over its heat
	capacity, so a 16 kg fitting with a metal's conductivity asks for twenty substeps while the
	armour around it asks for one. A profile granting six is integrating that block outside the
	range its own physics is stable in. MaxSubstepsPerBlock already floors exactly those blocks —
	see docs/field-tuning.md — and this is the other half: the properties a capacity floor cannot
	reach, and a balance rather than a tolerance.

	The "simulation" profile has no overlay, on purpose. It runs the shipped definitions exactly,
	so it stays the thing every other configuration is measured against, and so a benchmark
	cannot quietly become a comparison between two sets of definitions.

	An empty Subtype means every block, including the ones no definition file mentions - which on
	an ordinary world is most of them, and is where a stiffness problem usually lives. A named
	subtype refines that, and later entries win.
-->
<ThermalOverlay>
	<Note>Simulation's answer with the cost dials tuned. Nothing here changes where heat settles.</Note>

	<Blocks>
		<!--
			Decorative and electronic blocks fall through to the default entry and inherit mild
			steel on a 16 kg body, which is what makes the least massive block on a ship the
			stiffest thing on it. A light is a plastic housing around a glass lens; plastic is
			about 0.2 W/(m K) against steel's 50.
		-->
		<Block Subtype="InteriorLight">
			<Set Name="Conductivity" Value="2" />
			<Set Name="SpecificHeat" Value="900" />
		</Block>
		<Block Subtype="ReflectorLight">
			<Set Name="Conductivity" Value="2" />
			<Set Name="SpecificHeat" Value="900" />
		</Block>
		<Block Subtype="EmissiveBlock">
			<Set Name="Conductivity" Value="1" />
			<Set Name="SpecificHeat" Value="840" />
		</Block>
		<Block Subtype="CameraBlock">
			<Set Name="Conductivity" Value="5" />
			<Set Name="SpecificHeat" Value="800" />
		</Block>
	</Blocks>
</ThermalOverlay>
